    "answer": {
      "short": "Line (2) divides by $\\sin x$ without checking $\\sin x=0$, losing $x=0,\\pi,2\\pi$.",
      "worked": "The transition from line (1) to line (2) divides by $\\sin x$. This loses solutions for which $\\sin x=0$. Factor instead:\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin x\\cos x-\\sin x&=0\\\\\\sin x(2\\cos x-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\sin x=0$ or $\\cos x=\\frac12$. In the given interval, these give $x=0,\\pi,2\\pi$ or $x=\\frac\\pi3,\\frac{5\\pi}3$. The missing solutions are $0,\\pi,2\\pi$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
